(I was made to hit in America)

21
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:33,170
I was made to hit in America

22
00:01:43,050 --> 00:01:45,120
-Over there!
-Where?! Where?!

23
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,450
What?

24
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:50,990
It's a guy!

25
00:01:50,990 --> 00:01:55,190
Hey...When are you gonna
introduce me to your sister?

26
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,130
I see that you're good friends...

27
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:01,030
Ouch!

28
00:02:04,340 --> 00:02:06,570
Ouch!

29
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:10,980
Can he really sing?

30
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:13,850
Well, let's get to the studio
and start our session.

31
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:16,450
What? We're not going for drinks?

32
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:18,220
Listen, you...

33
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:20,990
Oh, well...I guess I'll
just have to belt it out.

34
00:02:20,990 --> 00:02:22,750
I'm looking forward to it.

35
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:27,020
-Okay, okay. Well, let's go.
-Yeah...

36
00:02:29,290 --> 00:02:34,230
"Hyodo and the Jaguar"

37
00:02:39,260 --> 00:02:41,560
I think I'll get out now.

38
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:42,830
Yeah...

39
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Won't you come out too, Koyuki?

40
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,590
Yeah...

41
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:05,510
Koyuki...

42
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:08,220
You can have this.

43
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:12,920
Why, this is...

44
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:18,100
It's the pick that
Eddy of the Dying Breed used.

45
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:23,640
But...isn't that important to you?

46
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:30,070
I picked it up at a performance
long ago. It's my treasure.

47
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:36,710
I can't accept this.

48
00:03:41,090 --> 00:03:43,630
Koyuki...

49
00:03:43,630 --> 00:03:46,030
Take good care of it!

50
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:56,300
Thanks!

51
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,790
Yeah...

52
00:04:11,550 --> 00:04:13,990
Sorry for calling you out so late at night.

53
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:18,890
Don't worry about it.
So, what did you want?

54
00:04:18,890 --> 00:04:24,300
I've been thinking about the band,
and I've reached a decision.

55
00:04:24,300 --> 00:04:25,600
And?

56
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:29,810
I've decided to join Ryusuke's band.

57
00:04:29,810 --> 00:04:33,400
Taira-kun...Are you serious?!

58
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:39,780
I've always made decisions
based on my instincts.

59
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:42,880
I've done everything I could...

60
00:04:45,290 --> 00:04:48,490
-It's magic...
-Magic?

61
00:04:48,490 --> 00:04:55,160
Ryusuke's band has the magic
I've been searching for.

62
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:58,700
See you around, Eiji.

63
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:11,370
Damn that Ryusuke!

64
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,310
Damn him!

65
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:26,650
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

66
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:36,910
Hey, Tanaka. I see some
sort of confidence in you lately.

67
00:05:36,910 --> 00:05:38,770
Oh...Really?

68
00:05:38,770 --> 00:05:42,310
Something must have happened.
Is it a girl?

69
00:05:42,310 --> 00:05:46,480
A girl? No, but I have learned
how to do the butterfly kick.

70
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:51,420
That girl wearing the No. 55 T-shirt
was so cute! A good singer, too!

71
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:56,260
-Oh, that's Maho-chan!
-Maho?

72
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:59,250
Come on! Introduce me, will you?!

73
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:11,810
Nishimoto-sensei is out on maternity leave,
so here is her replacement.

74
00:06:11,810 --> 00:06:14,140
Uh...Ogasawara-sensei!

75
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:25,050
Hello, everyone!

76
00:06:25,050 --> 00:06:30,320
Uh...I'm Momoko Ogasawara!
I'll be teaching music!

77
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:37,430
Since we're so close in age,
you can call me Momo-chan!

78
00:06:37,430 --> 00:06:40,090
-Awright!
-Momo-chan!

79
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:51,810
Man, that substitute is so hot!

80
00:06:51,810 --> 00:06:55,180
"Just call me Momo-tan!"

81
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:57,290
Hey, Tanaka, are you listening?!

82
00:06:57,290 --> 00:06:58,910
Over there...

83
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:05,880
Momo-chan!

84
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:09,390
Uhh, Sensei?

85
00:07:17,070 --> 00:07:20,980
-I feel like giving up teaching.
-Huh?!

86
00:07:20,980 --> 00:07:27,450
After all, no one listens
to me during class...

87
00:07:27,450 --> 00:07:32,120
I was listening! Really listening!
Right, Tanaka?!

88
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,720
I hear you're good at singing, Tanaka-kun!

89
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:39,760
-Where'd you hear that?
-I heard from Nishimoto-sensei.

90
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:43,730
This guy can really sing!
The other day, he...

91
00:07:43,730 --> 00:07:47,640
I've been put in charge of the
choir contest for the Culture Festival.

92
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:49,170
That's great!

93
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:54,140
I'd like you to lead
the class, Tanaka-kun!

94
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:59,100
-Eh? T-Tanaka-kun...
-Leading the class?

95
00:08:05,290 --> 00:08:08,360
I'm counting on you!

96
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,490
-Yes, ma'am!
-Yes, ma'am!

97
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:11,360
Thank you!

98
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,340
"Music Room"

99
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,340
"Light Music Club"

100
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:29,210
-If I could have any wish granted now,
-If I could have any wish granted now,
-If I could have any wish granted now,

101
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:36,280
-I'd want wings
-I'd want wings
-I'd want wings

102
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:41,820
-Say, isn't the soccer game today?
-I'm supposed to shop with Mariko!

103
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:44,460
I'm sorry. I have to go.

104
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:46,590
Come on! This is serious stuff!

105
00:08:46,590 --> 00:08:48,730
-Let's stop by Lotteria.
-Yeah!

106
00:08:48,730 --> 00:08:53,190
Momoko-sensei made this printout
for us! Let's memorize the lyrics-

107
00:08:58,940 --> 00:09:03,430
You're annoying. If you wanna
do this, why not do it yourself?

108
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:10,350
Everyone...Let's practice harder tomorrow!

109
00:09:10,350 --> 00:09:12,720
-What a ditz!
-Who has time for this?

110
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:15,890
I'll be waiting for you!

111
00:09:15,890 --> 00:09:17,720
I'll be waiting!

112
00:09:20,030 --> 00:09:22,500
Man, that was scary.

113
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:26,400
If Hyodo sets his sights on you,
you're in serious trouble.

114
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:29,730
If you go up against him, you're dead!

115
00:09:33,310 --> 00:09:36,340
Hey! Koyuki!

116
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:37,830
Izumi-chan!

117
00:09:39,280 --> 00:09:43,590
Did you hear? Ryusuke-kun's
new band finally has a name!

118
00:09:43,590 --> 00:09:46,590
His new band?

119
00:09:46,590 --> 00:09:48,960
Would you believe...it's Beck!

120
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:51,990
-His dog?
-Oh, that weird dog?

121
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:54,660
Chiba-kun had the bright idea!

122
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,800
He thought up all kinds of weird names

123
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:03,440
like Blue Lightning, Naked Devils,
and Dream Travelers.

124
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:06,500
-Get real!
-It's true!

125
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,980
You want to join the Light Music Club?

126
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:13,980
Maybe you shouldn't.

127
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:18,850
Why not? I thought I might make
some friends I can talk music with.

128
00:10:18,850 --> 00:10:23,830
But I haven't heard
anything good about that club.

129
00:10:23,830 --> 00:10:26,520
I haven't heard a thing, either.

130
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,200
"Music Room"

131
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,200
"Light Music Club"

132
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:44,680
"Cultural Festival"
"One Day Left"

133
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,810
Do you think we'll be ready
in time for the festival tomorrow?

134
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:47,580
Do you think we'll be ready
in time for the festival tomorrow?

135
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:49,220
We'll make sure we are.

136
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:51,050
Think our coffee shop will make money?

137
00:10:51,050 --> 00:10:53,380
No, let's offer curry!

138
00:10:57,430 --> 00:11:00,950
To think that no one's
practicing for tomorrow...

139
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:12,030
A Jaguar!

140
00:11:17,610 --> 00:11:21,020
And you know...

141
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:23,920
-Tanaka!
-Whattaya think you're doing?!

142
00:11:23,920 --> 00:11:27,160
-I'm sorry!
-I'll slap you upside your head!

143
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:31,430
But...This is a Jaguar, right?

144
00:11:31,430 --> 00:11:34,860
A Jaguar like the one
Kurt Cobain of Nirvana used.

145
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,260
-I've always wanted to play-
-Try playing it.

146
00:11:38,270 --> 00:11:40,000
You're sure?

147
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:20,440
What's with your playing?!

148
00:12:20,440 --> 00:12:24,480
Man, I can't stop laughing!

149
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:27,880
My sides hurt!

150
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:32,290
Listen. How long've you been playing?

151
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:36,360
Well, uh...since summer break.

152
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:40,400
I'm learning from a man named Saito-san.
He loves British rock.

153
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:42,730
Who the heck is Saito?

154
00:12:42,730 --> 00:12:48,600
If you learn from a nobody like him
you'll always be the butt of jokes.

155
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:55,710
You can laugh at me all you like!

156
00:12:55,710 --> 00:12:59,810
But could you stop insulting Saito-san?!

157
00:12:59,810 --> 00:13:01,720
Huh?!

158
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:05,020
You're a pain, you know? Damn you!

159
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:18,400
Hey, Tanaka...Do you know
whose Jaguar that is?

160
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,840
It wasn't my fault.

161
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:24,210
-He's about to start one behind the school!
-Start one?

162
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:29,800
Hey, Tanaka. I'll introduce
the owner of that Jaguar.

163
00:13:35,420 --> 00:13:39,720
What can I do? I don't
have what I don't have.

164
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:42,860
-That guy...
-It's Yonehara-sempai.

165
00:13:42,860 --> 00:13:45,660
No one could beat him
when he was in elementary school.

166
00:13:49,060 --> 00:13:52,730
D-don't tell me that was his guitar?

167
00:13:54,770 --> 00:13:56,670
Screw you!

168
00:14:03,180 --> 00:14:05,040
Don't take me for a fool!

169
00:14:07,650 --> 00:14:10,550
That's Rikiya Kitazawa...
my childhood friend.

170
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:11,790
Whoa...

171
00:14:11,790 --> 00:14:15,020
That fight was over money
borrowed for video games.

172
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:17,190
-Huh?!
-Which means...

173
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:22,060
What do you think'll happen
if he finds out about his Jaguar?

174
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:23,430
Huh?

175
00:14:23,430 --> 00:14:26,530
Hey, Masaru! You were watching?

176
00:14:26,530 --> 00:14:29,800
No, we just happened by.

177
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:32,900
Oh...Is that so?

178
00:14:52,590 --> 00:14:58,100
"A 14-year-old middle school student,
tired of being bullied at school,

179
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:00,930
used a tri-sectional staff from China and..."

180
00:15:07,480 --> 00:15:12,210
I didn't tell Rikiya-kun about you, for now.

181
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,720
Koyuki!

182
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:28,030
Oh...So it is you.
What's wrong? You look pale.

183
00:15:28,030 --> 00:15:31,870
Yeah...But I'm fine now!

184
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:34,300
Aren't you sweating a lot?

185
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:40,640
Ryusuke's in a recording studio right now.

186
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,780
Oh, with Beck?

187
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:47,180
Yeah...Won't you come watch with me?

188
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:51,580
But...He never wanted to see me again...

189
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,720
Koyuki, are you hungry?

190
00:15:56,720 --> 00:16:02,360
I, uh, treated someone earlier,
so I'm broke...

191
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:03,930
Want some fries?

192
00:16:03,930 --> 00:16:06,370
Oh, uh...Thanks...

193
00:16:08,470 --> 00:16:11,400
-Want a hamburger too?
-Yeah!

194
00:16:12,510 --> 00:16:16,170
Hurry up, will you?! Come on!

195
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,670
Koyuki!

196
00:16:19,810 --> 00:16:23,120
I'll just take a peek from here.

197
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:24,550
You serious?

198
00:16:24,550 --> 00:16:28,990
-Oh, that bassist-!
-Yeah. Taira-kun joined up.

199
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:33,060
Seems Ryusuke and Eiji
went head to head over it.

200
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:34,230
He did?

201
00:16:34,230 --> 00:16:37,830
Everyone looked all over for a drummer,

202
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:40,840
but in the end they settled
on Togo-san of Serial Mama.

203
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:43,900
Oh...That guy?

204
00:16:46,170 --> 00:16:48,810
They've been composing new songs,

205
00:16:48,810 --> 00:16:53,180
auditioning at live houses,
and sending out demo tapes.

206
00:16:57,790 --> 00:17:01,860
I've never seen Ryusuke so pumped up.

207
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:04,830
Koyuki? What's wrong?

208
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:07,190
I'm sorry!

209
00:17:10,300 --> 00:17:11,560
Koyuki?!

210
00:17:24,450 --> 00:17:27,570
I've gotta do something, too!

211
00:17:36,290 --> 00:17:38,630
Tanaka-kun?

212
00:17:38,630 --> 00:17:40,030
Momoko-sensei!

213
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:44,170
It's finally time for the choir contest!

214
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:48,370
I'm sorry I wasn't able to
live up to your expectations...

215
00:17:48,370 --> 00:17:49,640
Nonsense...

216
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,240
Tanaka-kun...Thank you.

217
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,310
Huh?

218
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:56,280
Let's sing with all our heart!

219
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:57,810
Sensei...

220
00:17:57,810 --> 00:17:58,800
Right!

221
00:17:59,650 --> 00:18:04,410
The 8th graders will sing "Give me Wings."

222
00:18:10,930 --> 00:18:17,700
-If I could have any wish granted now,
-If I could have any wish granted now,
-If I could have any wish granted now,

223
00:18:17,700 --> 00:18:30,340
-I'd want wings
-I'd want wings
-I'd want wings

224
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:38,750
Man...I didn't think we'd be that bad.

225
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:43,120
We came in last...
and Momoko-sensei cried...

226
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:46,260
Is that a guitar?

227
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:54,070
What is this?!

228
00:18:54,070 --> 00:18:56,130
They're having a wild time!

229
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,810
Oh! Look at all those girls!

230
00:19:00,810 --> 00:19:02,470
That guitar...

231
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:06,180
-It's Hyodo!
-You're right!

232
00:19:12,620 --> 00:19:15,280
Next year, let's do a concert...

233
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:23,090
Hyodo-kun...He's really good!

234
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:44,080
Hey...Tanaka.

235
00:19:45,390 --> 00:19:47,490
Hyodo-kun!

236
00:19:47,490 --> 00:19:49,520
Your live performance was great!

237
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:53,130
I was practicing an imaginary guitar!

238
00:19:53,130 --> 00:19:58,090
Go and buy me a cola, soy milk,
a melon roll, and a curry bun.

239
00:19:59,730 --> 00:20:05,070
Your encore was so exciting!
Even Kazuko-sensei was dancing!

240
00:20:05,070 --> 00:20:08,810
Bring them to the music room ASAP.

241
00:20:08,810 --> 00:20:11,910
I ran into Rikiya-kun earlier.

242
00:20:11,910 --> 00:20:16,450
He was steaming
about the scratch on the Jaguar.

243
00:20:16,450 --> 00:20:19,150
He's searching all over
for the one who did it.

244
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:26,290
T-that last song was
a cover of Springs, right?!

245
00:20:26,290 --> 00:20:32,100
Listen! I don't wanna talk music with you!

246
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:35,340
If you don't want me to tell
Rikiya-kun about the scratch,

247
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:38,310
you'd better hurry up and do as I say!

248
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:46,610
Screw that...He can't order me around.

249
00:20:46,610 --> 00:20:50,610
Hey! Rikiya-sempai's started a fight!

250
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:59,160
Hey, isn't that the Judo Club captain?!

251
00:21:11,070 --> 00:21:13,440
I'm in a bad mood today!

252
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:16,670
Don't complain just because
I skipped the room-cleaning!

253
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,520
Koyuki!

254
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:27,620
